[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1070,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 1086,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151426,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 36,
        "headingId": 1086,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Villous adenoma&nbsp;/ tubulovillous adenoma of the vagina is a primary benign glandular tumour resembling its colorectal counterpart.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:17:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1071,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 1087,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151427,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 36,
        "headingId": 1087,
        "headingText": "<font color=\"red\">Classification in progress, Data not available in this Beta</font>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:17:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1072,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 1088,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151428,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 36,
        "headingId": 1088,
        "headingText": "<font color=\"red\">Classification in progress, Data not available in this Beta</font>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:17:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1073,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 1089,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151429,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 36,
        "headingId": 1089,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> intestinal-type adenoma; adenomatous polyp.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:17:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1074,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 1090,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151430,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 36,
        "headingId": 1090,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:17:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1075,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1091,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151431,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 36,
        "headingId": 1091,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Various locations within the vagina have been reported; however, most occur along the lower posterior wall {24722061}. Rare cases have been described in the vulvar vestibule {36307835}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:17:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1076,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1092,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151432,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 36,
        "headingId": 1092,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most patients present with a vaginal mass or abnormal vaginal bleeding {24722061}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:17:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1077,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1093,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151433,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 36,
        "headingId": 1093,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are extremely rare vaginal lesions. They have been reported in adults aged 19&ndash;80&nbsp;years {24722061; 23202776}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:17:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1078,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1094,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151434,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 36,
        "headingId": 1094,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Speculated origins include intestinal metaplasia of the vaginal surface epithelium or adenosis, congenital rests of intestinal epithelium (cloacal remnants), and extension of intestinal epithelium through a rectovaginal fistula {24722061}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:17:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1079,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1095,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151435,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 36,
        "headingId": 1095,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A frameshift truncating mutation in <em>APC</em> has been reported in one adenoma, and mutations in <em>KRAS </em>and <em>TP53</em> have been reported in associated adenocarcinomas {30383609; 39522642}. <em>TP53</em>, <em>KEL</em>, <em>RB1</em>, <em>RNF43</em>, and <em>PTEN </em>mutations demonstrated high variant allele frequency in one case {36307835}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:17:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1086,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1102,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151436,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 36,
        "headingId": 1102,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are polypoid lesions, with reported cases measuring 9&ndash;30&nbsp;mm {24722061; 23202776}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:17:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1080,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1096,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151437,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 36,
        "headingId": 1096,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Histology shows villiform and/or tubular structures lined by columnar epithelium, often containing scattered goblet cells, with atypical pseudostratified elongated hyperchromatic nuclei {24722061}. No stromal invasion is present. The degree of atypia ranges from mild to severe. Cases with severe nuclear atypia and/or architectural complexity should be diagnosed as adenomas with high-grade dysplasia using the criteria applicable to their colorectal counterparts {24722061}. Immunohistochemically, they are usually positive for CK20 and CDX2; CK7 is variable, and ER is usually negative {24722061; 30383609}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:17:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1081,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1097,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151438,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 36,
        "headingId": 1097,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:17:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1082,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1098,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151439,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 36,
        "headingId": 1098,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:17:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1085,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 1101,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151440,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 36,
        "headingId": 1101,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> tubulovillous/villous architecture; intestinal-type epithelium with nuclear pseudostratification and hyperchromasia; no stromal invasion.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> presence of goblet cells; positivity for CK20 and/or CDX2.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:17:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1083,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 1099,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151441,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 36,
        "headingId": 1099,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are benign tumours and are not staged.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:17:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1084,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 1100,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151442,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 36,
        "headingId": 1100,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patient outcome may be uneventful; however, in some cases, the lesions may recur {24722061; 15661252}. One patient developed intestinal-type adenocarcinoma 2&nbsp;years after the diagnosis of adenoma with high-grade dysplasia {24722061}. The coexistence of intestinal-type adenocarcinoma with villous/tubulovillous adenoma suggests that the latter is a premalignant lesion similar to those that occur in the gastrointestinal tract {11293170; 16803550; 23202776; 24371679}. Metachronous vulvar tubulovillous adenoma has been reported in one case {30383609}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:17:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]